IMAGE A = the {{objectLabel}} reference photo (final, do not modify). IMAGE B = a reference photo of the décor/design element to composite onto the scene with IMAGE A.

{{GLOBAL_RULES}}

OBJECT IDENTITY LOCK: the {{objectLabel}} shown in IMAGE A must remain 100% visually unchanged: same wrap graphics, same colors, same logo, same wheels, same windows, same three-quarter angle and proportions. Do not repaint it, do not color-grade it, do not blend it into the scene lighting — it must be lit and rendered as its own independent, faithful subject, not stylistically merged with the background or the decor.

CRITICAL TEXT FIDELITY: every piece of text, lettering, and small badge/sticker/QR code printed on the {{objectLabel}}'s surface in IMAGE A must be reproduced pixel-for-pixel identical to the reference image — same letters, same spelling, same orientation, never mirrored, distorted, or substituted. If the decor element from IMAGE B would visually overlap any text or badge, shift its position slightly so the text stays fully legible and unobstructed instead of covering or altering it.

DECOR ELEMENT: use IMAGE B as the visual reference for the décor/design element's exact structure, colors, and materials — reproduce it faithfully, do not redesign it.

PLACEMENT: {{placementInstructions}}

{{scale_block}}

CRITICAL NO-OCCLUSION RULE: unless the placement instructions above explicitly say otherwise, the decor element must stand clear of the {{objectLabel}} — neither the decor structure nor any part of it may overlap, stand in front of, or cast a shadow across any part of the {{objectLabel}}'s body or its text/branding. Leave a visible gap of background between the decor and the {{objectLabel}} so its surface stays 100% unobstructed and legible.

BACKGROUND: clean, minimal studio-style background — soft white-to-very-light-gray gradient, subtle soft floor shadow beneath both the {{objectLabel}} and the decor element, matching the lighting and background style already present in IMAGE A. No people, no crowd, no unrelated staging elements beyond what is explicitly described above.

PHOTOGRAPHY: hyperrealistic, high-detail product/marketing photography, photoreal textures with soft specular highlights, sharp focus throughout, professional automotive-ad lighting quality, 8K, photorealistic depth of field.

{{notes_block}}
